Jonadab the Unsightly One wrote:
> Doug Freyburger wrote:
>
>> I also leave my main stash on the level above the one I am exploring and
>> then shuttle it to the down stairs when I finish a level.  Since it's on
>> a level that I am not on no movement happens so it's somewhat safe.
>
> Nothing happens on levels you're not on?

Correct.  Caveat - It might be that the position of monsters on a level
is randomized when you arrive there but there is no motion when you're
not on a level.

> Huh.  I would not have guessed that.

It's because the movement code is based on where you are.  It does not
scan all levels.

> A lot must happen in the time it
> takes me to get to and from the stairs sometimes.  Either that or rock
> moles can work a lot faster than I would have guessed, because a
> couple of times I have left a level looking more or less normal and
> returned later to find rather copious amounts of new tunnel.  I had
> assumed that the rock mole was being generated and doing most of its
> work while I was off-level.

Actually the digger was working out of line of sight back when you were
on that level.  I seen new tunnels all over the dungeon from diggers.

> Interesting -- and useful.

Very useful.  Without a container it does not reduce the danger to items
completely.  That's why I shuttle my stash to near the down stairs after
I have cleared a level.  It gives newly generated monsters much less
time to move around.  A gelantinous cube engulfing a stack of
valuables is a bad experience but they do move slowly.  Very few
monsters will approach a stack with an engraved E-word but they don't
last and burning an E-word per level as you explore down is very
expensive.

If I ever have a permenant stash location like a valkyrie using the Orb
to return to her stash, then I'll burn the E-word under my stash.

> Wait, how does the game know whether a pet left on a different level
> was getting enough to eat?

It calculates ages when you enter the level.  That's when corpses
disappear as well.  It would take a debugger or a level dumping program
to see the corpses on a level you're not on but they are there in the
data.

When you enter a level the pet's tameness and hunger are calculated the
turn you arrive on the level.


